<title>TURKEY: Turkey c.bank fx reserve down $532 mln last week.</title>
<headline>Turkey c.bank fx reserve down $532 mln last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves fell by $532 million to $16.249 billion in the week ended on September 13.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Sept 13	 Sept 6	  end-1995</p>
<p>Forex reserve  16.249	  16.781	   12.391</p>
<p>Gold reserve    1.383	   1.383	    1.383</p>
<p>Total reserve  17.632	  18.164	   13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose $481 million to $27.458 billion in the week ending August 30, the bank said.</p>
<p>It said Turkey serviced $509.91 million of state foreign debt in the period of September 2-18, bringing the total to $6.536 billion from January 1 to September 18, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom, 90-312-4462940 EKS</p>
